Six palettes, on their own axis (1.13.0)

Stone, Ocean, Forest, Sunset, Violet, Grey — picked as coloured dots in the
account menu, stored per browser like the light/dark choice.

The palette is a second axis, not a replacement: each one is defined for
both light and dark, so "Ocean + dark" is dark Ocean rather than one
setting overriding the other.

Each palette moves only the neutral hue and the primary. Neutral chroma
stays under 0.02 — past that a "warm theme" becomes a beige theme.
Destructive, success and warning keep their own hues everywhere, because a
palette should not change what red means.

The pre-paint script sets the palette too, not just light/dark. Without
that the page flashes the default palette before swapping.

